# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Prologue | Scene: OpeningScene

translate es strings:

    old "King Orwell has returned from his travels through the provinces of Rosanna."
    new "El Rey Orwell ha regresado de sus viajes por las provincias de Rosanna."

    old "He enters the great hall of Castle Reinmeer, the snow of an early winter drifting in behind him."
    new "Entra en la gran sala del castillo Reinmeer, con la nieve de un invierno temprano flotando tras él."

    old "Finally, home again."
    new "Finalmente, en casa otra vez."

    old "King Orwell pluts his travel bag down."
    new "El rey Orwell coloca su maleta de viaje sobre el suelo."

    old "FATHER!"
    new "¡PADRE!"

    old "Sarah leaps into her father's arms."
    new "Sarah se lanza en los brazos de su padre."

    old "Ooh, Sarah, my back! Please daugher, I'm not as young as I was, and you've grown much too big to just be jumping on me."
    new "Oh, Sarah, ¡mi espalda! Por favor, hija, no soy tan joven como antes, y has crecido demasiado para saltar sobre mí así."

    old "You were gone for almost five months! If you thought I wasn't going to hug you, you don't know me at all."
    new "¡Estuviste ausente casi cinco meses! Si creías que no te iba a abrazar, no me conoces en absoluto."

    old "You've grown older but I don't think you've grown up yet."
    new "Has envejecido, pero no creo que hayas madurado aún."

    old "So mean!"
    new "¡Tan cruel!"

    old "Speaking of growing up, have you seen..."
    new "Hablando de hacerse mayor, ¿has visto...?"

    old "DAD!"
    new "¡PAPÁ!"

    old "Thomas Rose, Sarah's younger brother, and heir to the throne, embraces his father."
    new "Thomas Rose, el hermano menor de Sarah y heredero del trono, abraza a su padre."

    old "I've missed you so much dad!"
    new "¡Te he extrañado tanto, padre!"

    old "King Orwell grabs his son by the shoulders and holds him at a distance."
    new "El rey Orwell agarra a su hijo por los hombros y lo mantiene a distancia."

    old "I missed you too son, but remember: composure. It's not befitting for a future king to be running around like a wild child."
    new "Te extrañaba también, hijo, pero recuerda: compostura. No le corresponde a un futuro rey correr por ahí como una cría salvaje."

    old "That goes for both of you."
    new "Eso aplica a los dos."

    old "King Orwell looks sternly at his daughter."
    new "El Rey Orwell mira severamente a su hija."

    old "Yes Father."
    new "Sí, Padre."

    old "Good. Now, where is the royal assistant? I need begin drafting letters immediately."
    new "Bien. Ahora, ¿dónde está el asistente real? Necesito comenzar a redactar cartas de inmediato."

    old "I think I saw him in the library, Father. I'll walk with you."
    new "Creo que lo vi en la biblioteca, Padre. Le acompañaré."

    old "Fine, fine. Thomas, find a servant to carry this luggage to my room. And don't let me catch you doing it yourself again."
    new "¡Bien, bien! Thomas, encuentra un sirviente para llevar este equipaje a mi habitación. Y no me pille haciéndolo tú otra vez."

    old "Yes, Father."
    new "Sí, padre."
